# LAN-only for now. The server sits behind NAT on a private address, so
# Let's Encrypt cannot reach it to solve the HTTP-01 challenge — the public
# 202.28.45.141 does not forward 80/443 here. Until we front this with a
# Cloudflare Tunnel (or get the ports DNAT'd), serve plain HTTP.
#
# The explicit http:// scheme is what disables Caddy's automatic HTTPS. Drop
# it and Caddy resumes trying to obtain a cert, which will fail on loop.
http://172-26-55-36.sslip.io, http://172.26.55.36 {
	reverse_proxy backend:8080
}
